# Build-time placeholders, not configuration.
#
# Next inlines every NEXT_PUBLIC_ value into the bundle as it builds, so the
# image is built against these sentinels and docker-entrypoint.sh swaps in the
# real values when the container starts. That is what lets one image run in any
# environment. The Dockerfile does not reference this file — `next build` picks
# it up itself, since NODE_ENV is production there.
#
# A sentinel is __NAME__ rather than the bare NAME so the entrypoint's sed
# cannot also rewrite a genuine mention of the variable in server code.
#
# Adding a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable means adding its line here.
#
# Locally this file is outranked by .env.local (Next reads
# .env.production.local, .env.local, .env.production, .env, first match wins),
# so `bun run build` still builds against your own values.

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=__NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL__
NEXT_PUBLIC_USER_POOL_ID=__NEXT_PUBLIC_USER_POOL_ID__
NEXT_PUBLIC_USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID=__NEXT_PUBLIC_USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID__
NEXT_PUBLIC_USER_POOL_DOMAIN=__NEXT_PUBLIC_USER_POOL_DOMAIN__
NEXT_PUBLIC_COGNITO_OAUTH_REDIRECT_SIGN_IN=__NEXT_PUBLIC_COGNITO_OAUTH_REDIRECT_SIGN_IN__
NEXT_PUBLIC_COGNITO_OAUTH_REDIRECT_SIGN_OUT=__NEXT_PUBLIC_COGNITO_OAUTH_REDIRECT_SIGN_OUT__
